  "description": "Verifies Z = ((1-Q^r)/(1-Q))^n, the principal specialisation of the classical sum_lambda f^lambda s_lambda = p_1^n, to <1e-30 for n=2..12. Since Q>1 and Q^r>1 make both 1-Q^r and 1-Q negative, the base is positive and sign(Z)=+1 for all n -- closing the residual global-sign hole left by #4662 and making sign(y_lambda) = (-1)^{P(lambda)} unconditional. Gated additionally on the summands being genuinely mixed-sign for n>=4, so the 'positivity is not term-by-term' claim is not vacuous -- and on the ONSET being exactly n=4 with sole negative (1,1,1,1), an independent confirmation of the >=4-row criterion of shallow_of_no_deep_cells (a negative weight needs a deep cell, a deep cell needs 4 rows).",
